meta {
  name: Generate Share Link
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/companies/:companyId/jobs/:jobId/share
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:path {
  companyId: 3ad4d39f-8a12-491e-8f7b-f0b371861622
  jobId: replace-with-job-id
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{accessToken}}
}

docs {
  Requires JwtAuthGuard + CompanyMemberGuard (no @RequiredRole, so any
  member of the company can generate a share link).

  Contract input is { companyId, jobId } from the path. Returns a URL:
  - If the job status is PUBLISHED, returns the public front-end job page
    URL directly (no token involved).
  - Otherwise, returns `${FRONTEND_URL}/jobs/shared/:shareToken`. A token
    is generated (and persisted, 48h expiry) only if none exists yet or
    the existing one has expired; otherwise the existing token is reused.

  That share link is deliberately unauthenticated: it's meant to be opened
  by people outside the company (see "Get Shared Job" below), so the
  backing endpoint lives on a separate controller with no guards.
}
